<title>NETHERLANDS: Heijmans, Holzmann win Dutch order.</title>
<headline>Heijmans, Holzmann win Dutch order.</headline>
<dateline>ROSMALEN, Netherlands 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Builder Heijmans NV said on Friday it and Germany's Philipp Holzmann AG had won an order to build a river lock near the village of Lith in the south-eastern Netherlands.</p>
<p>&quot;The total contracting sum is about 90 million guilders,&quot; the Dutch firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>The project will start in January and is expected to end in 1999.</p>
<p>Heijmans and Holzmann have previously cooperated in building bridges in the Netherlands.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
